	],
	"notes": [
		{
			"id": "nMEHU-wxBHaTM4cKZ",
			"text": "Typical Stats from the package record: ST 20, DX 10, IQ 13, HT 13, HP 25, WILL 16, PER 13, FP 16, SPEED 5.75, MOVE 5, DODGE 8, DR 2. GCS derives its own values by applying the ancestry; where the two differ, the package's Typical Stats are what the Dungeons on Automatic encounter tables use."
		},
		{
			"id": "npErjiIuW_b3KqIhp",
			"text": "Encounter rating: CER 60 (offense 24, protection 36), threat tier major, appearing 1."
		},
		{
			"id": "ngbHFdHT2nDMftU4n",
			"text": "Dreadful Glare: No attack roll and no active defense. Dreadful Glare (12): 1d-4 toxic, Reach Ranged, gaze. The tomb's own verdict on trespass. Fright Check at penalty; a badly failed roll leaves the victim paralyzed by dread as it closes."
		},
		{
			"id": "n59IgvvKKuwz8a2r7",
			"text": "GCS ancestry draft: gcs/mummy-lord.gct"
		},
		{
			"id": "nx0sAD2y1zXWbyyDY",
			"text": "Independent build total: 450 points of racial traits plus 16 points of racial skills."
		},
		{
			"id": "ny0JsCqFykGOKRMTw",
			"text": "Answers the SRD heading(s): Mummy Lord (SRD 5.1); Mummy Lord (SRD 3.5). Only the creature identity is taken from the SRD; the GURPS statistics, ratings and prose are this project's own work and reproduce no SRD text."
		},
		{
			"id": "nLHosrtTZRnmHJYf5",
			"text": "Typical Stats, damage and ratings are derived from the racial template, not authored beside it, so the sheet and the stat block cannot disagree."
		},
		{
			"id": "nyNpOuWd4l1m0izT6",
			"text": "Body mass used to scale this build: 60 kg. ST, Size Modifier and DR are checked against it; see the gurps-animal-sanity-check skill for the bands."
		},
		{
			"id": "nnDJeDxpg_I5P_Knm",
			"text": "Movement: ground Move 5 (primary). The published Move is the primary medium's cruising Move; sprint figures are stated here and not folded into it."
		},
		{
			"id": "nee7cD9WGntZAycZe",
			"text": "Treasure and grappling are not authored for this batch and ship as explicit nulls; `lair` carries a short habitat note, because where a wandering animal dens is an encounter fact rather than a loot one."
		},
		{
			"id": "nIFqWR4gXb9m6S_eJ",
			"text": "The rot is the identity and it is deliberately not survivable by attrition: the affliction points price a curse whose wounds cannot be healed until it is lifted, and the stat note says so in the GM's terms."
		},
		{
			"id": "nNNxqgwnO61vt29F9",
			"text": "Priestly magic is carried the same way the lich's wizardry is: Magery plus fatigue-costed attacks, with the full liturgy left to prose."
		},
		{
			"id": "naM25_7yhrPVGxbB8",
			"text": "Burning was the old answer and remains a good one; nothing here prices it away."
		},
		{
			"id": "nIwq9DMGzqyJhLNsT",
			"text": "Monster statistics, ratings and description prose by Monsters on Automatic; AI-generated first draft, project-reviewed, released under CC BY 4.0."
		}
	],
